WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.410
On the Port Campbell coast
of Victoria, Australia,

2
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:07.290
limestone, wind and waves
have shaped the shoreline.

3
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:12.670
One of its landmarks, London Bridge, was
a natural arch joined to the mainland.

4
00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.230
In 1990, it collapsed.

5
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.250
Two visitors were left on the new island,

6
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.090
until they were rescued by helicopter.

7
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.310
So how does the sea cut a piece of
coast free and turn it into an island?

8
00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.890
In this mission, you'll
see how waves attack rock,

9
00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:31.490
and why some coasts give
way faster than others.

10
00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:33.850
Then you'll read Dorset's
headlands and bays,

11
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.190
and watch a cliff retreat.

12
00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:41.170
Your mission: explain how the sea can
turn part of a headland into an island.
